Driver memory SHA-256: 89a390670f05984823cf4c5f0f7d25e3dedb7781fb65dd6c0c6ee22a273ad970
Runner SHA-256: 7e21043cd3429fbe97494a53936a82a2759a4fad40060289bf1ee415ddbb79c5 (zenbench ac675d3a, 0.1.10).
CUDA runtime: NVRTC/builtins 12.4.127, 204 package-owned headers, two real libraries, five loader aliases.
Scoped SDK manifest SHA-256: 39e2acdd0eb8b0dbd3372808aaeb8499e455b9691d94f975e2b05a1fe178da1f.
Each native bundle binds all SDK files and loader names by hash, using relative CUDA_PATH=sdk and LD_LIBRARY_PATH=sdk/lib64. The host supplies its own driver.
Control command: just iqa-gpu-check <binaries> cuda <new-controls> <exact-adapter-name>.
Deployment command: just iqa-gpu-deployment-bench <binaries> <runner> <controls> <new-output> <machine> <exact-domain> <scoped-sdk>.
Six variants: butteraugli-gpu, cvvdp-gpu, dssim-gpu, iwssim-gpu, ssim2-gpu, zensim-gpu.
Each: cold and warm_instance, 256x256 patterned RGB8, two calls; exact scalar products across packed/padded and ordinary/instrumented controls.
Both direct-control suites: 24/24 cases passed. This certifies functional determinism/layout/instrumentation on this fixture, not canonical metric accuracy.
Native worker cases: packed, both reuse modes, separate latency/os_peak and instrumented/driver passes; each receipt recovered by hash. Warm_instance retains metric buffers, not a cached reference. Cold can retain process-wide context/JIT caches between its two operations.
Resource boundary: outer hard system scope AllowedCPUs=2, MemoryMax=16G, MemorySwapMax=0; run-heavy inside. Resource receipt RSS describes the supervisor; committed records retain metric-child resident high water or Rust heap phase quantities. Device memory is not observed by this driver.
