i134 raw resolving path: ~/tmp/zm-iqa-cuda-20261012/{controls-recovered,fleet-observations,fleet-observations-v2}/.
i134 initially had an open 595.99.02 kernel module incompatible with Pascal. The proprietary 580.178.04 driver now recognizes the card. After hot replacement, udev repeatedly unloads/reloads NVIDIA modules; replacing the child unload actions with target-only rmmod reduces that loop, but the native campaign still observes intermittent initialization failures. The vendor rule is preserved at ~/tmp/zm-iqa-cuda-20261012/71-nvidia.rules.original; its SHA-256 is 0a6e1b3ba1c875d14402a1e136d16bf4db60da779096129976257a9bd5b0398e. A targeted override is installed at /etc/udev/rules.d/71-nvidia.rules. A reboot is awaiting operator approval; i134 CUDA worker deployment remains unqualified.
All failed attempts and raw logs remain retained. No assertion or tolerance changed. Performance observations are descriptive, with no speed acceptance.
